   "source": "tesseract-psm3",
   "text": "Comparative Growing Trials Agronomy\nAll characteristics and comparisons are from a comparative\ngrowing trial conducted at the Agricultural Research Centre, \u201cTaranna\u2019 is a perennial grass native to Australia and so should\nTamworth in 1990 and 1991. Transplanted seedlings were be adapted to dry conditions and low soil fertility. It is intended\nsown in the field on 16 July 1990. Plants were sown on a | for use in temperate areas either for aerial establishment into\nmetre square grid in 30 metre rows. Rows were randomly allo- non-arable, hilly country or as a pasture grass in degraded crop-\ncated among lines and each consisted of 3 replicates of 10 ping lands. It produces more growth in spring, early-summer\nplants of each line. Morphological characteristics were mea- than \u201cHume\u201d and has a high rate of seed retention.\nsured on cither 20 or 30 plants of each type. Plots were main-\ntained weed-free by cultivation, fertilised annually and watcred This work was supported by a grant from the Wool Research",
